---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import LifecycleNotice from "../../components/StandardLifecycleNotice.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/japangaap/asbj03.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope — What This Amendment Historically Addressed" },
        { id: "s3", label: "The Staged Reform Process — Statements No. 3, 14, and 19" },
        { id: "s4", label: "What Statement No. 3 Historically Changed" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Why It Was Abolished — Absorption Into ASBJ Statement No. 26" },
        { id: "s6", label: "The Current Standard — ASBJ Statement No. 26" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Worked Example — the Historical Reform in Outline" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Disclosure Requirements (Current, Post-Abolition)" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Critical Judgments" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS — Then and Now" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <LifecycleNotice
    type="historical-reference"
    explanation="ASBJ Statement No. 3 was a transitional partial amendment to Japan's retirement benefits accounting, issued as part of a staged reform process. It has since been abolished (廃止) and its substance fully absorbed into the comprehensive ASBJ Statement No. 26, Accounting Standard for Retirement Benefits — the current, authoritative J-GAAP retirement benefits standard."
    historical="This poster is retained for historical reference and to explain the staged reform process that led to today's standard."
    link="/japangaap/asbj26"
    linkText="ASBJ Statement No. 26 — Accounting Standard for Retirement Benefits"
  />

  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A staged, incremental path toward today's comprehensive standard</div>
        <div class="principle">Japan's retirement benefits accounting REFORM did NOT arrive as a single, comprehensive standard all at once — instead, it was introduced through a SERIES of PARTIAL amendments issued over time (ASBJ Statements No. 3, No. 14, and No. 19), each addressing a SPECIFIC aspect of retirement benefit accounting, BEFORE the ASBJ ultimately consolidated the reform into the SINGLE, comprehensive <strong>ASBJ Statement No. 26</strong> — the standard now in force. Statement No. 3 represented an EARLY stage in this INCREMENTAL reform journey.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — What This Amendment Historically Addressed</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Companies sponsoring retirement benefit plans for employees</div>
        <div class="principle">Like its successor standards, ASBJ Statement No. 3 HISTORICALLY applied to companies sponsoring RETIREMENT BENEFIT plans (both defined benefit pension arrangements and lump-sum retirement allowance plans, a distinctively COMMON Japanese practice) for their employees.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>The Staged Reform Process — Statements No. 3, 14, and 19</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Three successive partial amendments, each building on the last</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-1-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Historical role</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-1-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 3</span><span>An EARLY partial amendment addressing specific retirement benefit measurement/disclosure matters — NOW ABOLISHED</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-1-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 14</span><span>A FURTHER partial amendment (Part 2) — ALSO now abolished</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-1-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 19</span><span>A THIRD partial amendment (Part 3) — this one has REMAINED referenced (not abolished in the same way), reflecting the staged nature of the reform</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="note">This staged, multi-part amendment approach is a genuinely DISTINCTIVE feature of J-GAAP standard-setting history — reflecting a preference for INCREMENTAL reform, allowing preparers TIME to adjust to changes before a fully comprehensive standard was finalised.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>What Statement No. 3 Historically Changed</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">An early step toward more consistent retirement benefit accounting</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">As an EARLY-STAGE partial amendment, Statement No. 3 addressed SPECIFIC, NARROWER aspects of retirement benefit accounting current at the time — REFINING particular measurement or disclosure practices WITHOUT yet establishing the FULL, comprehensive framework that ASBJ Statement No. 26 would eventually provide. Its content has since been ENTIRELY absorbed, refined, and superseded by later stages of the reform.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Why It Was Abolished — Absorption Into ASBJ Statement No. 26</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Consolidation into a single, comprehensive standard</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">Once the ASBJ completed its COMPREHENSIVE reform of retirement benefit accounting — culminating in <strong>ASBJ Statement No. 26, Accounting Standard for Retirement Benefits</strong> — the EARLIER, PIECEMEAL partial amendments (including Statement No. 3) became REDUNDANT, since their substance was FULLY incorporated (and, where appropriate, further developed) within the new comprehensive standard. The ASBJ therefore ABOLISHED (廃止) Statement No. 3, consistent with GOOD standard-setting practice of avoiding overlapping, superseded guidance remaining formally in force.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>The Current Standard — ASBJ Statement No. 26</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Today's authoritative retirement benefits framework</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">ASBJ Statement No. 26 is the CURRENT, comprehensive J-GAAP retirement benefits standard — addressing recognition and measurement of retirement benefit obligations (退職給付債務), plan assets, actuarial gains/losses, past service cost, and the presentation of net retirement benefit liabilities/assets on the Balance Sheet — broadly analogous in SCOPE to IAS 19 (Employee Benefits) internationally, though developed through Japan's OWN staged reform history rather than as a single comprehensive project from the outset.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Worked Example — the Historical Reform in Outline</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Tracing a company through the staged reform</div>
        <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A company's retirement benefit accounting across the reform period</div><div class="wk-body">A Japanese company sponsoring a lump-sum retirement allowance plan applied EARLIER retirement benefit guidance, then Statement No. 3's partial amendment, then Statements No. 14 and No. 19's further amendments, over a period of ongoing standard-setting reform.</div><div class="wk-answer">TODAY, the SAME company simply applies <strong>ASBJ Statement No. 26</strong> in its ENTIRETY — the comprehensive successor standard that has absorbed and superseded the ENTIRE staged reform history, including the NOW-ABOLISHED Statement No. 3 — with NO need to separately reference the earlier partial amendments.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements (Current, Post-Abolition)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What applies today instead</div><div class="check-list"><span>Full compliance with ASBJ Statement No. 26's recognition, measurement, and disclosure requirements</span><span>No separate reference to the now-abolished Statement No. 3 is required or appropriate</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Critical Judgments</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most (historically and today)</div>
        <div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">HISTORICAL JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Correctly sequencing application of the staged partial amendments during the reform period</span></div></div>
        <div><div class="elabel">CURRENT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Actuarial assumptions and measurement judgements now governed entirely by ASBJ Statement No. 26</span></div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS — Then and Now</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Convergence-driven reform, mirroring the broader ASBJ-IASB project</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">The STAGED retirement benefits reform (Statements No. 3, 14, 19, culminating in No. 26) took place LARGELY within the CONTEXT of the ASBJ's BROADER convergence project with the IASB, launched in 2005 — progressively bringing J-GAAP's retirement benefit accounting CLOSER to IAS 19's principles (e.g. recognising net retirement benefit obligations more fully on the Balance Sheet, refining actuarial gain/loss treatment) over SUCCESSIVE stages, rather than through a single, immediate wholesale adoption. This INCREMENTAL convergence PATTERN is itself a notable, recurring feature of how J-GAAP has approached international alignment across MANY topic areas, not just retirement benefits.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where retirement benefit accounting now lands</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Retirement benefit obligation and plan assets</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span></span><span>Governed entirely by the current ASBJ Statement No. 26</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 26</span><span>Successor, comprehensive standard — the current authoritative J-GAAP retirement benefits framework</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 14 / 19</span><span>Related staged amendments from the same reform history</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Retirement benefit obligation (退職給付債務)</div><div class="glossary-def">A company's actuarially determined obligation for employee retirement benefits, now governed comprehensively by ASBJ Statement No. 26.</div></div>
        <div class="glossary-item glossary-item--last"><div class="glossary-term">Abolished (廃止)</div><div class="glossary-def">The formal ASBJ status indicating a standard's substance has been fully absorbed into a successor standard, with the original no longer separately in force.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表) <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書) <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部 <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書) <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)</div></div>

  </div>
</StandardPageLayout>
